{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793651926,"nonce":"FXeybRuJ4aRSazOPgYj3bhVaqno=","title":"Allow synced sandbox sessions to reach their configured gateway","message":"Parent: cd54ac37bbbdfea0fa1fcd39288738a7c0b48475ed9ecea3e6cc98ad20c109ed.\n\nThe runner gives restored sessions a write-back capability, but both image and toolchain-snapshot guests have Network::None, so publishing cannot reach the gateway. Select a deny-by-default host allowlist only for synced workspaces. Keep ordinary GitHub workspaces offline; apply the same policy to toolchain restores and compute replacement.\n\nThe runner may fetch from a loopback development gateway on its host, which is not the same address from a VM. Allow an optional operator-configured syncGateway.guestUrl pointing to the same gateway's HTTPS endpoint, inject only that guest address into the session, and derive the single allowlisted host with a URL parser. Reject credentials, queries, fragments, wildcards and invalid/insecure public URLs; reject guest loopback/unspecified addresses before allocating compute. Keep the provisioning secret on the host.\n\nVerify configuration and both launch paths with the runner suite. Use the quiet NUC's MSB 0.7.11 to confirm that the allowed host connects while unrelated DNS and IP destinations remain blocked. Full account-authenticated publication against real Cloudflare remains a deployment check. Existing no-network guests are not silently destroyed or recreated when this code is installed.","files":null}]}